# Nightly public-holidays refresh — crontab entry for the deployment host.
#
# Install (as the user that owns the checkout, no root needed):
#     crontab -l | grep -v refresh_holidays | cat - deploy/holidays-refresh.cron | crontab -
#
# What it does: refreshes the public-holidays register from Nager.Date (the
# authority) with the LLM filling Arabic names and proposing the Islamic holidays
# Nager does not carry. The service is idempotent, so a night with nothing new
# writes nothing — the log line will read "no changes".
#
# Database: this entry deliberately sets NO database flag. The job must use the
# same database as the web process, and on a real host that comes from the
# project's own .env (POSTGRES_*). The local dev machine runs its server with
# DJANGO_USE_SQLITE=1, so its crontab entry carries that prefix — do not copy
# that flag to a server.
#
# Logs: point the redirect at a path the service user can write. A non-zero exit
# means Nager was unreachable and nothing was written; a warning line means the
# LLM was down but the official import still landed.

# m  h  dom mon dow   command
0    0  *   *   *     cd /srv/tracking_system/backend && .venv/bin/python manage.py refresh_holidays >> /srv/tracking_system/backend/logs/holidays-refresh.log 2>&1
